meta {
  name: Register
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/auth/register
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "first_name": "علی",
    "last_name": "رضایی",
    "mobile": "09123456789",
    "otp": "123456",
    "password": "password123"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  const responseBody = res.getBody();
  const payload = responseBody;

  if (res.getStatus() === 201 && payload?.access_token) {
    bru.setEnvVar("access_token", payload.access_token);
  } else {
    bru.deleteEnvVar("access_token");
  }
}

docs {
  ## Purpose

  Creates a new account after verifying the registration OTP.

  ## Authentication

  Public endpoint.

  ## Behavior

  - A valid OTP requested with the `register` purpose is required.
  - The returned access token represents the new Better Auth session.
  - The mobile number must not already belong to an existing account.
  - The user's basic profile is created using the provided first and last name.
  - First and last names are required trimmed strings, each limited to 1,000 UTF-16 code units. Name validation runs before consuming the OTP or creating an account.
  - Password is required and must satisfy the configured password policy.
  - Password policy is checked before the valid OTP is consumed.
  - A successful registration authenticates the newly created user.
  - The access token is returned in the response.
  - The session is also issued in an HttpOnly cookie.

  - A bounded single-process per-identity authentication attempt limiter also applies.

  ## Response

  - `201 Created` — Account created and authentication completed successfully.
  - `400 Bad Request` — Request validation failed, the mobile number is already registered, the OTP is invalid, or the password does not satisfy the password policy.
  - `429 Too Many Requests` — Authentication attempt limit reached.
  - `500 Internal Server Error` — Unexpected provider or database failure; generic translated message and `X-Request-Id`, with no exception details.
}
